# `--allocator debug` is a leak verdict source of its own
# (plans/backlog/ZIG_ADOPTION_CANDIDATES.md Z11): a
# `pragma(Pragma.NeedsLeakVerdict)` file must RUN under it even when no
# AddressSanitizer test binary is built (`--disable-sanitize`, a wasm
# target), instead of being skipped as "would pass vacuously". The fixture
# leaks, so the run fails: the verdict is real, not vacuous.
stdout_keep_match=(Skipping .*|✓ .*|✗ .*|Memory leak detected:|live at exit: [0-9]+ blocks / [0-9]+ bytes|[0-9]+ passed|[0-9]+ failed)
timeout=600
